course: dictionary
lesson: 4767
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is the context. «She was a busy housewife, cooking and cleaning all day for her family.» The clues are busy, cooking, cleaning and family, so housewife means a woman who looks after her home and family.
explain: Old meanings can still appear in books and history. In old British English, a housewife could also be a small sewing kit, also spelled «hussif». The sentence tells you which meaning is meant: a sewing kit cannot cook or clean, so it is not a person.
explain: Today many people say «homemaker» or «stay-at-home parent» instead, because these words can describe a man or a woman. The joking name «domestic engineer» means much the same thing, so you can swap these words in a sentence and check that the meaning still makes sense.
fact: Housewife is a noun. One is a housewife, and more than one are housewives.
fact: «Housewife» means a woman whose main work is looking after her home and family, not working at a paid job.
fact: In old British English, «housewife» can also mean a small sewing kit, also spelled «hussif».
fact: Today many people say «homemaker» or «stay-at-home parent», because these words can be used for a man or a woman.
fact: «Domestic engineer» is a joking name for a housewife, househusband or homemaker.
exercise: «She was a busy housewife, cooking and cleaning all day.» What does housewife mean here? | A teacher at a school | A shop that sells food | *A woman who looks after her home and family | A small sewing kit
exercise: Ruby finds a tiny case with needles and thread, and the label says «hussif». What is it? | A busy housewife | A petrol station | *A small sewing kit | A loaf of bread
exercise: Why do many people today say «homemaker» instead of housewife? | Because homemaker means a paid job in an office | Because homemaker is an old word for a sewing kit | Because housewife is never used in any book | *Because it can describe a man or a woman
test: «"Domestic engineer" is a joking name for a housewife, househusband or homemaker.» What does the word joking tell you? | It is a real job title for engineers | It means a sewing kit | *It is a funny nickname, not a real job title | It means a shop that sells tools
test: Which is the plural of housewife? | *housewives | housewifes | housewivess | housewife's
exam: Which sentence uses housewife to mean a small sewing kit? | "The housewife was tired after a long day at work." | "My neighbour is a housewife and looks after three children." | *"Grandma kept a hussif full of needles and thread in her bag." | "The housewife in the story cooked dinner every night."
